=== layout: one-panel

# Check the Double-Crossover Types

@body

Arrange the alleles in *map order: A-J-E*.

{table-style=testcross}
| Type | A | J | E | Count |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Parent | a | j | + | 2,112 |
| DCO | a | [*+*]{background-color=#ece6ff} | + | 47 |
| Parent | + | + | e | 2,088 |
| DCO | + | [*j*]{background-color=#ece6ff} | e | 23 |

Only the middle gene, J, changes relative to the matching parent.
In the homework's A/E/J columns, the DCO types are *a++* and *+ej*.

